From 03ae4680c7b0d72bc2fa115d4384f6a8b9443619 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vikas soni <vikassoni@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:07:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-121098: Improper state validation in GPU

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444381:
[GPU Security] Improve GPU fence handle validation and lifetime.

Validate file descriptor duplication in PlatformDuplicate() and
GLFenceAndroidNativeFenceSync::CreateFromGpuFenceHandle() so invalid
descriptors are not passed to eglCreateSyncKHR(). Close the released
file descriptor if CreateInternal() fails so it does not leak.

Also check for null GLFence or GpuFence returns in
GLTexturePassthroughOzoneImageRepresentation::BeginAccess(),
    VideoImageReaderImageBacking::VideoRepresentation::BeginReadAccess(),
CommandBufferProxyImpl::CreateGpuFence(), and
GLES2CommandBufferStub::GetGpuFenceHandle().

Bug: 516958782
Change-Id: I528de20fed0196678c01a10e0fc2ea824471491f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444381
